* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text

# Layer-ratchet baselines (#329): machine-written violation records, never line-reviewed.
# `linguist-generated` is what scripts/pr-hygiene.logic.mjs reads to keep them out of the budget.
# Kept that way on purpose (#406): a baseline write rewrites the whole file, so a line review sees
# churn rather than meaning. What pays for the lost review is pr-hygiene's `ratchet` rule, which
# reads the rows against the PR's merge base — both files, the second as `(file, rule id)` rows
# whose count may only rise under a rule id the PR newly names in eslint.config.js (#429).
.dependency-cruiser-known-violations.json linguist-generated
eslint-suppressions.json linguist-generated

# Append-only records whose rows are independent single lines: two PRs that each add a row merge
# by keeping both, so a local rebase or `gh pr update-branch` no longer stops on them (#334).
# Not for DECISIONS.md or docs/decisions/rulings/*.md: those hold multi-line sections, and a union
# merge would interleave two edits of one section without warning.
docs/harness/ledger.md merge=union
